  "text": "proprium.sanctissimae-trinitatis-epistola",
  "about": "The Epistle of the feast of the Most Holy Trinity, Romans 11:33–36. The Apostle praises the unsearchable wisdom of God, from whom, through whom, and in whom are all things.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "O the depth of the riches of the wisdom and knowledge of God! How incomprehensible are His judgments, and how unsearchable His ways!" },
    "s02": { "translation": "For who hath known the mind of the Lord?" },
    "s03": { "translation": "Or who hath been His counselor?" },
    "s04": { "translation": "Or who hath first given to Him, and recompense shall be made him?" },
    "s05": { "translation": "For of Him, and by Him, and in Him are all things: to Him be glory for ever. Amen." }
  },
